{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/604297-ghouls-and-time","id":604297,"title":"Ghouls and Time","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-26T16:44:23-07:00","id":604297,"title":"Ghouls and Time","content":"Have I been mistaken for the last 11 years? And that ghouls do not need the monthly blood infusion form a master to stay a ghoul?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3640-gwiber","name":"gwiber","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T17:41:51-07:00","id":604338,"title":"","content":"They consume 1 Vitae a month to stay ghouled in Requiem. If they don't have it in their system when re-up time comes, they become Deprived and start aging again, rapidly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T03:36:41-07:00","id":604571,"title":"","content":"I think 2e removed the willpower requirement from upkeep though, so they could theoretically go stamina (+ resilience? I'm not too clear one way or the other) months without drinking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T06:09:57-07:00","id":606511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/604297-ghouls-and-time?p=604338#post604338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They consume 1 Vitae a month to stay ghouled in Requiem. If they don't have it in their system when re-up time comes, they become Deprived and start aging again, rapidly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not as bad as in OWoD. 1 year per week in Blood &amp; Smoke. To stop this the ghoul Must imbibe number of vitae equal to the blood potency of the vamp he last fed from.<br /> As I read it if last fed from a BP3 vamp and goes into withdraw he needs 3 vitae to stop the aging.<br /> p 297 Blood &amp; Smoke<br /> <br /> As to The original question Ghouls in Blood &amp; Smoke consumes a point from their vitae pool once a month.<br /> They can store their Stamina in Vitae (chart p. 90)as they are BP 0(p. 297).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":594,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","user":"Chattnos","date":". 07-29-2015, 09:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T23:22:38-07:00","id":608991,"title":"","content":"Okay that's different from the old system, Then now matter the amount of blood they had in their system at the end of a month, it &quot;Dried up&quot; so to speak, and they became mortal again. Vampires were able to keep ghouls on a much, much, tighter leash that way back in cWoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3640-gwiber","name":"gwiber","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T02:47:36-07:00","id":609190,"title":"","content":"Requiem ghouls are just better off in general than the masquerade sort. Better disciplines, more forgiving feeding schedule, bigger vitae pool (most of the time), you name it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T05:52:48-07:00","id":609293,"title":"","content":"In a chronicle of mine almost the whole group decided to play Ghouls, only one used a vampire. The &quot;coterie&quot; doesn't faced nearly as much power loss as it would in Masquerade. Indeed, they became one of the most feared in the city after some time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T21:40:00-07:00","id":610377,"title":"","content":"Requiem ghouls in 1st ed needed vitae and willpower from a vampire once a month. 2nd ed ghouls only need the 1 wp to make them a ghoul, and at least 1 vitae. After that, each month requires 1 vitae. If they have it in their system already, it's spent, if they don't, they have to get it from a vampire.<br /> <br /> So, in 1e, ghouls need to see a vampire at least once a month. In 2e, with a high enough stamina, they can go a few months before needing to feed from a vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T04:18:24-07:00","id":610652,"title":"","content":"<br /> Actually that's reversed. In 1st edition, a ghoul could spend the willpower themself each month and so long as they spent the willpower and had vitae in their system they remained a ghoul.<br /> In Blood and Smoke, they cease being a ghoul if they don't get at least one vitae a month. (But the monthly willpower expense is gone, its only needed by the vampire the first time.) And, they can't use disciplines if they are afflicted with the deprived condition (not enough vitae to eliminate vitae withdrawal.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T05:38:00-07:00","id":610702,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure in 1e the willpower had to be spent <i>as</i> the ghoul was ingesting vitae. Basically you needed to re-do the initial creation each month. Now it sticks around as long as you have vitae to spend, like how a vampire works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T15:20:38-07:00","id":612641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/604297-ghouls-and-time?p=610702#post610702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure in 1e the willpower had to be spent <i>as</i> the ghoul was ingesting vitae. Basically you needed to re-do the initial creation each month. Now it sticks around as long as you have vitae to spend, like how a vampire works.</div> </div> </div> </div>I concur with the your assertion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T21:33:48-07:00","id":613008,"title":"","content":"In 1st ed, the ghoul could spend the WP when they drank vitae from a vampire, but only if they know they can do that, and most vampires either don't know or don't tell them (to create dependence). Basically, yes, as others said, you have to &quot;create&quot; the ghoul every month with 1 wp and 1 vitae.<br /> <br /> 2nd ed, once they are created with the 1 wp and 1 vitae, from that point on they just need 1 vitae to spend every month to maintain being a ghoul, there is no more spending wp for upkeep. They can either drink the vitae from a vampire, or spend their own if they had more than 1 at the end of their month.<br /> <br /> So no, not reversed, that's exactly what I said the first time, just in different words.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T10:17:23-07:00","id":613612,"title":"","content":"This is what you said that I'm refuting.<br /> <br /> &quot;So, in 1e, ghouls need to see a vampire at least once a month. In 2e, with a high enough stamina, they can go a few months before needing to feed from a vampire.&quot;<br /> <br /> No they can't go a few months without tasting vitae, which they could do in 1st edition if the ghoul spent the willpower. In 2nd edition if, if a ghoul goes one month without getting vitae they immediately lose access to their disciplines and any vitae spending ability they had as a ghoul. Not only that, but if they don't get vitae amount equal or exceeding the blood potency the regnant from their last fix, the ghoul STILL can't use their abilities. While this is an effective deterrent to prevent neonates from easily stealing ghouls from their elders, yet allows an elder to steal from a younger, it also eliminates the oh I only need 1 vitae a month to viably maintain my ghoul mentality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 08-03-2015, 01:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T11:09:11-07:00","id":613687,"title":"","content":"They need one vitae <i>per</i> month, not one vitae <i>each</i> month. The rules make that quite clear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T17:29:33-07:00","id":614317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amaterasu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/604297-ghouls-and-time?p=613008#post613008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2nd ed, once they are created with the 1 wp and 1 vitae, from that point on they just need 1 vitae to spend every month to maintain being a ghoul, there is no more spending wp for upkeep. They can either drink the vitae from a vampire, or spend their own if they had more than 1 at the end of their month.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>A ghoul with 5 stamina could hold 5 Vitae... So This particular ghoul could go 5 months without feeding before running in to ghoul problems... Addiction problems are something quite different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T17:36:57-07:00","id":615797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/604297-ghouls-and-time?p=613612#post613612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is what you said that I'm refuting.<br /> <br /> &quot;So, in 1e, ghouls need to see a vampire at least once a month. In 2e, with a high enough stamina, they can go a few months before needing to feed from a vampire.&quot;<br /> <br /> No they can't go a few months without tasting vitae, which they could do in 1st edition if the ghoul spent the willpower. In 2nd edition if, if a ghoul goes one month without getting vitae they immediately lose access to their disciplines and any vitae spending ability they had as a ghoul. Not only that, but if they don't get vitae amount equal or exceeding the blood potency the regnant from their last fix, the ghoul STILL can't use their abilities. While this is an effective deterrent to prevent neonates from easily stealing ghouls from their elders, yet allows an elder to steal from a younger, it also eliminates the oh I only need 1 vitae a month to viably maintain my ghoul mentality.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;<span style=\"font-family:inherit\">As to The original question Ghouls in Blood &amp; Smoke consumes a point from their vitae pool once a month.</span> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">They can store their Stamina in Vitae (chart p. 90)as they are BP 0(p. 297).&quot; -me<br /> <br /> Go reread the ghoul section. They consume one vitae from their pool each month. They cease being a ghoul when they have no vitae.<br /> <br /> </span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T18:52:27-07:00","id":615892,"title":"","content":"Do you mean this section from page 100 of Blood and Smoke that says this:<br /> <br /> <i>In humans, Kindred Vitae teases at the gifts of the Requiem. When mortals taste Kindred blood, Kindred can give them a hint of their power. These mortals are called ghouls. They enjoy limited access to certain Kindred advantages. They quickly heal wounds, no longer age, and exhibit increased physical potency. They may even use some Disciplines. However, these gifts are fleeting; they depend completely on the ghoul\u2019s continued reliance on Kindred Vitae. <b>If a ghoul goes without for a month, she loses all these gifts as if she never had them.</b></i><br /> <br /> <br /> Or this, from page 297 and 298 of Blood and Smoke:<br /> <br /> <i>A ghoul automatically spends one point of Vitae per month to maintain his ghoul state. If, at the end of the month, he has no Vitae to spend, he must somehow acquire more. Any Vitae a ghoul imbibes becomes part of his Vitae pool. If a ghoul doesn\u2019t get his fix, he gains the Deprived Condition (see p. 302). In withdrawal, he begins to age towards his natural age, at a rate of one year per week. This aging remains even if he gets his fix and resolves the Deprived Condition. To end his withdrawal and resolve the Deprived Condition, he must ingest a number of Vitae equal to the Blood Potency of the last vampire he dosed from. If this is more Vitae than his Stamina dots allow him to hold, he retches the rest up violently, but resolves the Condition and is no longer in withdrawal. <b>A ghoul in withdrawal cannot use any Disciplines (even those that do not cost Vitae or which have persistent effects), but retains knowledge of them if his withdrawal ends.</b></i><br /> <br /> <br /> I don't see anything anywhere in Blood and Smoke that says a ghoul remains a ghoul so long as they have vitae. I see it expressly stating and reiterating that if they <u>don't</u> get vitae at least once a month, in addition to the accelerated aging and multiple attribute reductions they get from the deprived condition, they lose the use of their vampiric powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T19:21:35-07:00","id":615913,"title":"","content":"Funny, because you yourself just now quoted something somewhere in Blood and Smoke that says such.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/604297-ghouls-and-time?p=615892#post615892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or this, from page 297 and 298 of Blood and Smoke:<br /> <br /> <i><b>A ghoul automatically spends one point of Vitae per month to maintain his ghoul state. If, at the end of the month, he has no Vitae to spend, he must somehow acquire more. Any Vitae a ghoul imbibes becomes part of his Vitae pool.</b> If a ghoul doesn\u2019t get his fix, he gains the Deprived Condition (see p. 302). In withdrawal, he begins to age towards his natural age, at a rate of one year per week. This aging remains even if he gets his fix and resolves the Deprived Condition. To end his withdrawal and resolve the Deprived Condition, he must ingest a number of Vitae equal to the Blood Potency of the last vampire he dosed from. If this is more Vitae than his Stamina dots allow him to hold, he retches the rest up violently, but resolves the Condition and is no longer in withdrawal. A ghoul in withdrawal cannot use any Disciplines (even those that do not cost Vitae or which have persistent effects), but retains knowledge of them if his withdrawal ends.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Weird how moving a little bolding goes from allegedly supporting your position to supporting the other guy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":".  personal attack removed. Further attacks will result in suspension. 08-05-2015, 01:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T21:14:42-07:00","id":615969,"title":"","content":"VTR 1st ed, p. 167.<br /> <br /> &quot;A ghoul requires at least one Vitae per month to sustain the state of ghouldom. When receiving this monthly \u201cupkeep,\u201d either the vampire or the ghoul player must spend a point of Willpower. The Vitae need not come from the Kindred who initially created the ghoul. For the Kindred, this is a gamble. If the vampire player spends the Willpower point and/or Vitae herself, and the vampire never lets the ghoul know he can spend his own Willpower, the ghoul acquires a sense of expense associated with using that Willpower and Vitae. On the other hand, if the Kindred lets her ghoul know that he can spend the Willpower himself, she sets herself up for possible betrayal. If a vampiric master relies upon other Kindred to supply her ghouls\u2019 Vitae, those ghouls may eventually become subject to a Vinculum to another Kindred, which isn\u2019t always in the first Kindred\u2019s best interests.<br /> <br /> A ghoul who does not receive his monthly infusion of blood slowly returns to his previous mortal state.&quot;<br /> <br /> Each month the Ghoul must get vitae from a vampire. They cannot spend or use their own vitae. Thus they must interact with a vampire at least once a month to obtain this vitae. It does not matter if they have 0 or 10 vitae in their own system. They must take in 1 point of vitae from a Kindred, and the WP spend can be done by the vampire or the ghoul, <i>if</i> the ghoul knows they can do that. But the only variable is who can spend the WP. The Vitae must come from a vampire each month.<br /> <br /> So no, in 1st ed, a ghoul could not go more than a month just because they had vitae in their system.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T22:05:27-07:00","id":615999,"title":"","content":"It makes sense how they changed it given how Vampire 2e assigns a lot more agency to Ghouls and spends a bunch of time talking about how dangerous it can be to treat your ghoul like absolute shit all the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T22:36:57-07:00","id":616012,"title":"","content":"I am just a poor boy. Though my story's seldom told, I have squandered my resistance. For a pocket full of mumbles, such are promises all lies and jest. Still, a man hears what he wants to hear and disregards the rest. - The Boxer by Simon and Garfunkel<br /> <br /> We are all poor boys sometimes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T17:11:29-07:00","id":618233,"title":"","content":"Summary: the Ghoul needs just to have Vitae in her body as long as she doesn't enters withdrawal. If she have 5 Vitae, she can potentially go for months without any more.<br /> <br /> Actually, by the way, not 5 months, but SIX: she becomes a Ghoul until end of month just for imbibing Vitae, so she'll have all five points the next months to burn for a month longer Ghoul state per point.<br /> <br /> Once she enters withdrawal, though, she looses it all until fed a sizable amount of Vitae. With she once more don't need to actually spend at the time, so the first month of re-Ghouling is for free!<br /> <br /> Without the WP cost for upkeep, and other changes done, Ghouls can be a force by themselves, what is a theme they did introduced, so everything seems right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T22:16:31-07:00","id":618503,"title":"","content":"Of course, to have that, it means they have Stamina 5. Add in Resilience and that's a pretty beefy ghoul right there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}